From: turbo-boo <59400127+turbo-boo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:15:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Use AOSP runtime permission flow

HyperOS delegates its first-use CTA to SecurityCenter. AOSP has no handler for
that intent, leaving mIsNewCTAShowing set and causing every later camera setup
to be skipped. Mark the vendor CTA as already handled so Camera continues with
its normal Android runtime-permission checks.
---
 smali_classes4/da/a.smali | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes4/da/a.smali b/smali_classes4/da/a.smali
index ea917446..0d07e216 100644
--- a/smali_classes4/da/a.smali
+++ b/smali_classes4/da/a.smali
@@ -221,6 +221,10 @@
 .method public final c()Z
     .locals 2
 
+    const/4 p0, 0x1
+
+    return p0
+
     invoke-static {}, Lka/d;->a()Lka/a;
 
     move-result-object p0
